# Google Drive Sync Optimization Plan

This document outlines the proposed changes to resolve the issues inside Google Drive synchronization ([src/drive/sync.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js)), effectively addressing the folder duplication (39 vs 43 folders) and slow sync performance.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> By default, the current sync behavior is pure "append only" (never deletes). The new implementation will introduce **Mirror Deletions** for 1-way syncs. This means if a file/folder is deleted in the Source Drive, it will also be deleted in the Destination Drive. Please confirm if this is the desired behavior for 1-way syncs. Bidirectional sync will preserve files on both sides to avoid accidental data loss unless requested otherwise.

## Proposed Changes

### Drive Sync Logic updates [src/drive/sync.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js)
We will rewrite the [syncFolder](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#76-128) and supporting Google Drive API wrapper functions:

1. **Unique File Tracking via `appProperties` (Solves duplicates / Rename bugs)**
   - Update [listFiles](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#23-45) to also fetch `appProperties`.
   - Update [copyFile](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#46-60) and [createFolder](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#61-75) to embed metadata: `appProperties: { sourceId: fileId }`.
   - When matching source files to destination files, we will match primarily by `appProperties.sourceId`.
   - If a source file matches by `sourceId` but the names differ, it securely updates the destination file's name (resolving folder renames seamlessly).

2. **Mirror Deletion (Solves "ghost" folders accumulating)**
   - Add a `mirror` Boolean parameter to [syncFolder](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#76-128) (Default: `true` for one-way syncs, `false` for bidirectional).
   - After processing all source files, iterate over existing destination files. If a destination file was NOT found in the source files, issue a `driveService.files.update` to move it to trash (`trashed: true`).

3. **Parallel Processing (Solves slow sync speed)**
   - Instead of standard `for...of` loops causing sequential uploads/creations, we'll implement a fast chunk-based parallel executor.
   - We will run [copyFile](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#46-60) and [createFolder](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js#61-75) concurrently with a limit of 5-10 operations at a time to maximize speed while respecting Google Drive's API limits.
   
#### [MODIFY] [sync.js](file:///e:/TDC_App/TDGAMES_App/Sync_Slack_Discord_ClickUp_Drive/src/drive/sync.js)

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
*Currently no automated test suites configured.*

### Manual Verification
1. Open the project and start the server using `npm run dev`.
2. Find an active `Drive_Configs` record in NocoDB.
3. Rename a folder in the Client's source drive, run sync, and observe that it renames the Dest folder instead of creating a duplicate.
4. Delete a file in the Source drive, run the sync, and verify the corresponding file on our end is sent to the trash.
5. Check terminal logs to note the improved parallel speed of uploads.
